Z||000000||Steven||06-14-2001||06:32 PM||||Well what do you think? 96 GMC S-10 with stock 4.3 liter Vortec, and some kind of trans shift module that make it shift harder vs. 85 Pontiac Fiero GT with newly rebuilt 2.8 engine bored and stroked to 3.2. The Fiero was built using Crane .423/.423 cam. Compression is 8.5:1 also has ported and polished head. Stock manifolds that are also ported hooked up to factory exhuast (minus the cat.),  4 speed manual trans. The guy at work is wanting to race, and I don't even have the motor in the car yet. Hopefully it will go in tonight. Well what do you think? The S-10 or the Fiero GT? <P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shaun41178||06-14-2001||09:12 PM||||You will take him easy.  Don't sweat it.  My friend had the same kind of truck with a manual tranny and I raced him in my stock 2.8 auto with 100k miles on the engine.  I had him off the line by about half a car and held it up to about 45 and then he would start to slowly pull even with me.  Never got over 60 mph.  Close everytime.  <P>You have a ton of engine mods and a 4 spd so you will rip him a new one.  If I were you I would put money on it or a 6 pack just to make it more interesting<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
